                <pb facs="0546" n="450" sameAs="frus:frus1872p1/pg450"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Belknap to Mr.
                            Fish.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">War
                                Department</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic">Washington
                            City</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1872-08-07"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">August</hi> 7, 1872</date>. (Received August
                        9.)</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In connection with copies of papers
                    relative to the Howard’s Well massacre, transmitted to you in communication from
                    this Department of May 22 and July 19, 1872, I have the honor to send you
                    herewith copy of a letter from Major G. W. Schofield, Tenth Cavalry, commanding
                    Fort Hill, Indian Territory, upon the same subject.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully, &amp;c,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WM. W. BELKNAP,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of
                        War.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
